  <main id="main-content">
    <div class="legal-page">
      <span class="section-label">Legal</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: August 16, 2026</p>

      <p>The Greater Lowell Area Science-based Skeptics (GLASS) respects your privacy. This policy explains what
        personal data we collect through this website, why, how long we keep it, and the rights you have over it
        under the UK/EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and similar laws.</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>GLASS is an informal community group based in the Greater Lowell area of Massachusetts, USA. For any
        question about this policy or your data, contact us at
        <a href="mailto:info@sciencebasedskeptics.com">info@sciencebasedskeptics.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Account data</strong> — email address, display name, and a securely hashed password (we never
          store or have access to your password in plain text) when you register for an account.</li>
        <li><strong>Event reminder preferences</strong> — which reminder timings (e.g. 7 days before, 2 days before,
          the day of) you've opted into for upcoming GLASS events, and whether you've confirmed that opt-in via the
          link we email you. None by default; only set if you check the box at signup or choose timings from your
          account page, and reminder emails don't start until you confirm.</li>
        <li><strong>Session cookie</strong> — a single strictly-necessary cookie (<code>sid</code>) that keeps you
          logged in. It is not used for tracking or advertising, and no consent banner is required for it under
          ePrivacy rules. We do not use analytics or advertising cookies.</li>
        <li><strong>Contact form submissions</strong> — if you use the contact form, your name, email, and message
          are sent directly to our form processor, Web3Forms, and forwarded to us by email. We don't store these
          submissions in our own database.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why we process it, and on what basis</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Providing your account</strong> (email, name, password) — necessary to perform our contract
          with you as a registered member (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR).</li>
        <li><strong>Event reminder emails</strong> — your explicit consent, given by checking the opt-in box and then
          confirming via the emailed link (double opt-in) (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR). You can withdraw it any time from your
          <a href="/account">account page</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Keeping you logged in / account security</strong> — our legitimate interest in running a
          functioning, secure website (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).</li>
        <li><strong>Responding to contact form messages</strong> — your consent, given by submitting the form.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
      <p>We use a small number of third-party processors to run the site. Data may be processed on servers located
        in the United States.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Namecheap Private Email</strong> — sends account verification, password-reset, and event
          reminder (including confirmation) emails.</li>
        <li><strong>Web3Forms</strong> — delivers contact form submissions to us by email.</li>
        <li><strong>Turso</strong> — hosts our database (account records, sessions, tokens).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell your data, and we don't share it with anyone for marketing purposes.</p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Account data is kept until you delete your account or ask us to.</li>
        <li>Login sessions expire automatically after 30 days.</li>
        <li>Email verification and reminder-confirmation links expire after 24 hours; password reset links after 1
          hour. Expired or used tokens are purged automatically.</li>
        <li>An account that never verifies its email is automatically deleted after 30 days.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under GDPR you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Access</strong> the personal data we hold about you.</li>
        <li><strong>Correct</strong> inaccurate data.</li>
        <li><strong>Erase</strong> your data ("right to be forgotten").</li>
        <li><strong>Export</strong> your data in a portable format.</li>
        <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> (e.g. event reminders) at any time.</li>
        <li><strong>Object</strong> to processing based on legitimate interest.</li>
        <li><strong>Lodge a complaint</strong> with your local data protection supervisory authority.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You can exercise most of these yourself, any time, from your <a href="/account">account page</a>: download
        a copy of your data, or permanently delete your account. For anything else, email us at
        <a href="mailto:info@sciencebasedskeptics.com">info@sciencebasedskeptics.com</a> and we'll respond within
        30 days.</p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>This site is not directed at children, and we don't knowingly collect data from anyone under 16.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>If we make material changes to how we handle your data, we'll update this page and change the "last
        updated" date above.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
